.TH KRISTATECH-TX "1" "November 2026" "kristatech-tx v1.5.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kristatech-tx \- manual page for kristatech-tx v1.5.9.0
.SH DESCRIPTION
KristaTech kristatech\-tx utility version v1.5.9.0
.SS "Usage:"
.TP
kristatech\-tx [options] <hex\-tx> [commands]
Update hex\-encoded kristatech transaction
.TP
kristatech\-tx [options] \-create [commands]
Create hex\-encoded kristatech transaction
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\-?
.IP
This help message
.HP
\fB\-create\fR
.IP
Create new, empty TX.
.HP
\fB\-json\fR
.IP
Select JSON output
.HP
\fB\-txid\fR
.IP
Output only the hex\-encoded transaction id of the resultant transaction.
.HP
\fB\-regtest\fR
.IP
Enter regression test mode, which uses a special chain in which blocks
can be solved instantly.
.HP
\fB\-testnet\fR
.IP
Use the test network
.SH COMMANDS
.HP
\fBdelin=\fRN
.IP
Delete input N from TX
.HP
\fBdelout=\fRN
.IP
Delete output N from TX
.HP
\fBin=\fRTXID:VOUT
.IP
Add input to TX
.HP
\fBlocktime=\fRN
.IP
Set TX lock time to N
.HP
\fBnversion=\fRN
.IP
Set TX version to N
.HP
\fBoutaddr=\fRVALUE:ADDRESS
.IP
Add address\-based output to TX
.HP
\fBoutscript=\fRVALUE:SCRIPT
.IP
Add raw script output to TX
.HP
\fBsign=\fRSIGHASH\-FLAGS
.IP
Add zero or more signatures to transaction. This command requires JSON
registers:prevtxs=JSON object, privatekeys=JSON object. See
signrawtransaction docs for format of sighash flags, JSON objects.
.SH REGISTER COMMANDS
.HP
\fBload=\fRNAME:FILENAME
.IP
Load JSON file FILENAME into register NAME
.HP
\fBset=\fRNAME:JSON\-STRING
.IP
Set register NAME to given JSON\-STRING
